# Blender pipeline intermediates — regenerable, and large.
#
# Everything here is produced deterministically by the scripts in
# Tools/blender/exercises/ (see ANIMATION_HANDOFF.md). Only two outputs are
# actually needed downstream, and neither lives here:
#   * the .mp4 loops, which ship in Resources/Animations/
#   * the .py scripts that produce them, which are the real source of truth
#
# Regenerate any of this with:
#   /Applications/Blender.app/Contents/MacOS/Blender -b \
#       --python "Tools/blender/exercises/<name>.py"
#
# One batch of 14 exercises produced ~529 MB of these files, so they are not
# committed. Files tracked before this rule was added stay tracked; run
# `git rm --cached` on them if you want to stop carrying them too.

_demo_frames*/
*.blend
*.blend1
*.glb
*_log.txt
*_peak_demo.png
*_peak_front.png
*_rest_demo.png
